1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ridefogde på Herrevadskloster 1658. Ridefogde på Skillinge 1664. Ridefogde i Bjäre 1676. Kronobefallningsman i Bjäre 1673-1677.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Tabell 53 (generation 1)  (Från Tabell 1, s *) Rafn (Iversen enl. Ragnar Odhnoff), Wulf. Ridefogde på Herrevadskloster 1658. Ridefogde på Skillinge 1664. Ridefogde i Bjäre 1676. Kronobefallningsman i Bjäre 1673-1677. Läs mer om Wu
2 CONC lf Gift med Kock, Ottilie. Barn:
2 CONT * Rafn, Rasmus. Se tabell 54, s *.
2 CONT * Rafn, Corfitz. Ryttmästare i Jylland, Danmark. Se tabell 64, s *.
2 CONT * Wulfsdotter Rafn, Eleonora Christina. Död 1718 i Helsingborg (M). Se tabell 70, s *.
2 CONT * Wulfsdotter, Anna Catharina. Se tabell 75, s *.
2 CONT * Wulfsdotter, Ellna. Se tabell 76, s *.
2 CONT
2 CONT Met om Wulf Ravn: http://w1.401.telia.com/~u40107259/rafn/wulf.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Wulff was a well-known figure in Scanian history and quite controversial, too. His family were first clients of the Ulfeldt family and agreed to accept Swedish overlordship when the Swedes won the wars of 1657-1660  and the whole 
2 CONC Ravn family worked for them. When war broke out again in 1675, Wulff sided openly with the Danes and took service as a Danish "herredsfoged" in northwestern Scania. When the Danish navy arrived he sent a message to the admirals, o
2 CONC ffering them fresh lobsters from the Kullen peninsula. 
