1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugh_Percy,_10th_Duke_of_Northumberland
2 CONT
2 CONT * Lord Lieutenant of Northumberland from 1956 to 1984.
2 CONT * Chancellor of the University of Newcastle from 1964 to 1988.
2 CONT * Chairman of the Medical Research Council from 1969 to 1977.
2 CONT * President of the Royal Agricultural Society of England in 1956 and 1962
2 CONT * Chairman of the Agricultural Research Council from 1958 1968.
2 CONT * Chairman of the Committee of Enquiry on Foot and Mouth Disease.
2 CONT * Lord Steward of H.M. Household from 1973 to 1988.
2 CONT * Master of the Percy Foxhounds from 1940 to 1988.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was commissioned into the Northumberland Hussars. In 1940, as a Lieutenant, he transferred to the Royal Artillery. In 1947, as a Captain, he transferred back to the Northumberland Hussars.
