1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Petersen, Carol Augusta (Oleson) Born on December 29, 1917 on a farm near Lake Marion, south of Hutchinson, MN. She was the daughter of Ray and Anna (Johnson) Oleson and was baptized April 21, 1918 at St. Morton's 
2 CONC Lutheran Church, Heatwole. On March 20, 1932 Carol, together with siblings Russell and Fern, was confirmed at Main Street Lutheran Church. After High School graduation with the Hutchinson class of 1935, she earned a Bachelor of Ed
2 CONC ucation degree at Dana College and Mankato State Teacher's College. She taught at Le Seur and Redwood Falls, Minnesota as well as Aurora, Colorado and St. Francis, Kansas. Carol married Emery L. Petersen of Brush, CO on December 2
2 CONC 9, 1942. They served Lutheran Parishes in Iowa, Colorado, Kansas, Missouri, and during retirement, several interim ministries including a year at Jackson , WY. Those forty years were special as Carol's life was focused on family, 
2 CONC serving in delightful communities, and travels. Carol was preceded in death by her husband, Emery; her parents, Ray and Anna Oleson, brothers Russell and Roger Oleson, sisters Opal Oleson and Betty Myhr. Survivors include daughter
2 CONC s, Naomi Theye (Wayne), Sharon Holdorf, Ann Lee (Wayne), Ardis Nelson ( Mark) and grand- children, Jaron (Kirsten) and Dellan Theye; Kirsten (Steven) Roenfeldt, Peter (Jane) Nelson, Elizabeth (Jeremy) Hallquist, Ingrid Lee and gre
2 CONC at-grandsons, Henry Maxwell Theye and Axel Jens Roenfeldt. She is also survived by sisters Fern Oleson, Lois (Roger) Krantz and sister-in-law Lucille Oleson and many nieces and nephews. A memorial service will be on Wednesday, Jan
2 CONC uary 12, 2011, at St. John's Lutheran Church, 331 Harrison St. W., Annandale, MN at 11 am. In lieu of flowers, memorials preferred to Bread for the World. Published in Star Tribune on January 9, 2011
