1 OCCU Carpenter
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Married to Lillian Delight Beard August 7, 1933.  Born to two Danish immigrant parents.
2 CONT
2 CONT OBITUARY
2 CONT
2 CONT HENRY GUNDERSEN
2 CONT
2 CONT Services for Henry A. Gundersen will be Friday 2 p.m., at Kercheval Funeral Home, Sheridan, where friends may call after 2 p.m. tomorrow.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gundersen, 73, 303 West 2nd Street, Sheridan, a retired carpenter, died yesterday at Riverview Hospital.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a native of New York City, born Sept. 10, 1907, the son of Henrik Amund and Jensine Christine (Poulsen) Gundersen.  He lived in Sheridan for 32 years and was a member of Local 60 Brothers of Carpenters and Jointers.  He bel
2 CONC onged to the Danish Lutheran Church in New York City.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife, the former Delight Beard, survives, as do two daughters, Mrs. Alda D. Lovell, Springfield, VA, and Mrs. Betty Lee Cooper, Zionsville.  There are five grandchildren and one great granddaughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Three brothers are deceased.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial will be in Crown View Cemetery.  The Rev. Don Hoffman and Pastor Ron Reeder will perform the rites. Inscription: Married August 7, 1933
2 CONT * Reference: [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=43202990 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 21 2016, 17:31:09 UTC''
