0 @I346243974430005382@ INDI
1 NAME Edward John /Rayner/ Jr.
2 GIVN Edward John
2 SURN Rayner
2 NSFX Jr.
2 _MARNM Rayner
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 29 APR 1805
2 ADDR
3 STAE London
3 CTRY England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 14 AUG 1840
2 ADDR
3 CITY tiltons creek
3 STAE PEI
3 CTRY Canada
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Edward John Rayner has been a mystery.  He is frequently confused with his brother John, beause his birth occurred while the family was moving about in England.  I did find a christening record on familysearch.org 
2 CONC listing a birthdate of 29  Apr 1805 with christening at St Giles Church, Crippplegate, London of 22 June 1806.  The parents match, and documentation from family states moves from Little Wratting to London during that timeframe.  
2 CONT   Edward's mother has been rumored to be a daughter of King George III, however family genealogists have found that his mother was Mary Watson, born of a non-conformist family in Suffolk, near the Cambridgeshire border.  This line
2 CONC age follows back and can be established with records found in England.  
2 CONT   It is unknown as to when the Raynors arrived at PEI, and where the money came from to secure their home on Lot 18.  No records can be found to my knowlege.
2 CONT   Edward died young in 1840 and left a will that can be seen on Islandregister.com.  In it several Cannon's are of note.  When widow Elizabeth remarried John Wood, witnesses included Cannon's and Rayner's.  After this point, many 
2 CONC of Edward's children fall off the radar, as Elizabeth Wood continued to have Wood children.  My relative, Alfred Raynor was their last child and was unknown to some of the family.  I had his christening record to support my claim.
2 CONC   He is lost on the record until he appears on the Bangor Maine census in 1860.  I have no Idea who raised him, he talks of his parents relocating to Maine, but obviously this was not the case.  Alfred could not read or write, so 
2 CONC he left little record of his passing until he moved to Wisconsin.  I feel he lost contact with the PEI family.  At one point he spent 3 years in the north woods surveying lumber interests.  He then daughtered out and the Raynor na
2 CONC me died out in Wisconsin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth and Christening record - England Births and Christenings 1538-1975.  Indexing project batch C02577-9, England ODM, Source film #380209.
2 CONT --------------------
